  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Haitian rock-and-Vodou-fusion genre developed in late-1970s-1980s Haiti. Fusion of Haitian Vodou ceremonial-drumming-and-singing with rock-and-roots-music aesthetic. Emerged through Boukman Eksperyans (founded 1978 in Port-au-Prince by Theodore \"Lolo\" Beaubrun) and parallel groups Boukan Ginen, Sanba Yo, Rara Machine. Electric guitars-bass-drum-kit alongside Vodou-ceremonial percussion. The 1990 Vodou Adjae album consolidated international visibility.",
